NVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
PROJECT DOCUMENTATION

1. Project Overview
The Inventory Management System is a web-based application designed to help users manage and monitor items stored in an inventory. It allows users to add, view, update, delete, and track item quantities.

The system aims to make inventory management easier, more organized, and more accurate.

2. Objectives
- To create a simple inventory management system.
- To store inventory records permanently in a database.
- To make adding, editing, and deleting items easier.
- To monitor available item quantities.
- To reduce manual inventory recording.

3. Technologies Used
HTML – Used to create the structure of the website.

CSS – Used to style the website.

JavaScript – Used to add interactive functions.

PHP – Used for backend processing and communication with the database.

SQLite – Used to store inventory information permanently.

4. System Features
1. Dashboard
- Displays inventory information.
- Shows the total number of items.
- Shows available stock.
- Displays low-stock items.

2. Item Management
- Add new inventory items.
- View existing items.
- Edit item information.
- Delete inventory records.

3. Stock Management
- Add stock quantities.
- Reduce stock quantities.
- Display current available quantities.

4. Search Function
- Search for items by name or item code.

5. Low-Stock Notification
- Identify items with low quantities.
- Display low-stock reminders.
- Notify users when items need restocking.

6. Database Storage
- Stores inventory information permanently.
- Retrieves saved records when the system is opened again.

5. Inventory Information
Each inventory record may contain:
- Item ID
- Item Name
- Item Code
- Description
- Quantity
- Unit Price
- Date Added
- Time Added
- Minimum Stock Level

6. System Workflow
1. The user opens the inventory website.
2. The system retrieves inventory records from the database.
3. The user can add, edit, delete, or search for items.
4. PHP processes the submitted information.
5. SQLite stores or updates the records.
6. The updated inventory is displayed on the website.

7. Database
The system uses SQLite to store inventory information.

Database Table:
id - Unique item identifier
item_name - Name of the item
item_code - Item identification code
description - Item details
quantity - Available stock
unit_price - Price per item
minimum_stock - Minimum stock level
date_added - Date the item was registered

8. Development Environment
- Visual Studio Code – Code editor
- PHP – Backend programming
- PHP Built-in Development Server (still not sure kung id-deploy ba or locally)
- SQLite – Database management
- Web Browser – Displays the website

9. Expected Output
The finished system should allow users to manage inventory records through a simple website. Changes made to inventory records should be saved in the database and remain available after closing and reopening the website.

10. Conclusion
The Inventory Management System provides a simple way to organize and monitor inventory records. By using PHP and SQLite, the system can process information and store records permanently, making inventory management more convenient and efficient.
